laurel 2200: Mi A3 touch: FT3518 / GT9883 at panel resolution, TLMM edge latch, HID map from the framebuffer layout. topaz scaled the FT5452 grid 0..1349 x 0..2999 to 1080x2400 with 2-bit fractions from byte 4, and SweetHID.cpp normalized with /1080 /2400 and the 1080x2400 offsets in the iPhone X canvas. The Mi A3 (laurel_sprout-trinket-touchscreen.dtsi) has FocalTech FT3518 at 0x38 (display-coords 0 0 720 1560; byte 4 is the pressure) or Goodix GT9883 at 0x5d (goodix_gtx8 Normandy, panel-max 720x1560: event block 0x4100, 8-byte LE records, u8 checksum, handshake write 0). The boot of 2026-11-01 03:52 logged touches up to y=1247 after topaz's 4/5 scale = raw 1559: the FT3518 reports panel pixels. Raw -> panel pixels (PE_current_console); one log line if a raw value leaves the DT grid (moves once to 1350x3000 / 1080x2400). Any answer at 0x38 selects FocalTech (chip id reads 54:52 here, 35:18 in the Linux table); 0x5d without the GT9896 id selects GT9883. GPIO 88 falling edge latched in TLMM INTR_STATUS (raw status on, no summary interrupt), the thread reads on the latch / finger down / every 100 ms; the latch turns itself off after 3 touches found with no edge (poll 10 ms). SweetHID.cpp maps panel pixels with the layout SweetFramebuffer.cpp reports (sweet_hid_set_geometry: off + panel * num / den; default = the framebuffer's own formula on the console size), clamps and edge zones scale with the panel, SurfaceWidth/Height 65x140 mm. Lines: `LAUREL TOUCH: on: <vendor> <rawW>x<rawH> -> 720x1560, ...`, `LAUREL TOUCH: display map: panel 720x1560 at X,Y of WxH (scale 1/1)`. Kill switches unchanged: sweettouch=0, sweettouchirq=0 (latch off, poll).

